Alembic migrations for the Plumbing Marketing API.

Layout
  alembic.ini              config (URL comes from app settings, not here)
  migrations/env.py        loads DATABASE_URL from app.core.config, targets
                           app.db.base.target_metadata (Base.metadata)
  migrations/versions/     revision files (0001_initial_schema.py, ...)

Common commands (run from the project root, with DATABASE_URL set)
  alembic upgrade head                         apply all migrations
  alembic downgrade -1                         roll back one revision
  alembic downgrade base                       roll back everything
  alembic current                              show the applied revision
  alembic history --verbose                    show the revision graph
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "msg"     create a new revision from model diffs
  alembic upgrade head --sql                   print SQL without touching the DB

Notes
  - The app runs async (asyncpg); Alembic runs sync (psycopg). Both DSNs are
    derived from the single DATABASE_URL in app settings.
  - After editing models, run autogenerate, then READ the generated file before
    committing — autogenerate is a draft, not gospel (it can miss server-side
    defaults, partial indexes, and data migrations).
